-### RoDynRF
-**Definition:** Enables dynamic scene reconstruction from monocular videos without known camera poses by jointly optimizing intrinsics, extrinsics, and both static and dynamic radiance fields [S1].
-**Steps:** Introduce a two-branch architecture separating background and moving regions [S1]. Use motion masks to exclude dynamic pixels during pose estimation [S1]. Employ a coarse-to-fine voxel optimization scheme for stability [S1]. Use a time-conditioned deformation network to model non-rigid motion [S1].
+Test-Time Two-Stage Optimization is a post-training evaluation procedure that first optimizes camera poses and then optimizes appearance embeddings to handle unconstrained image collections with varying lighting and transient objects. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods by decoupling pose refinement and appearance adaptation into two sequential stages, addressing the limitations of methods that optimize only poses (e.g., BARF) or only appearance (e.g., NeRF-W).
 
